# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Ad-hoc coverage profiles (go test -coverprofile=reactor.cov ...) left
# behind by local runs and audit sessions; the gate's own profile is
# written to a temp path, never the repo root
*.cov

# The rendered half of the same habit: `go tool cover -func > cover.txt`,
# `go tool cover -html -o cover.html`, and a redirected `go test -bench`
# capture. Ignored rather than deleted — they are an audit session's in-flight
# evidence (§17 教训一: the scene outlives the verdict), and the repo never
# loses them because the numbers worth keeping get transcribed into
# docs/Benchmark.md and docs/NOTES.md, while the CI soak posts its own log as
# a run artifact
/cover.txt
/cover.html
/bench_*.txt

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum
.idea

# VitePress 文档站：依赖与构建产物只在本地/CI 存在，永不入库
#（pnpm install 与 vitepress build 都在仓库根跑，见 package.json 与
# .github/workflows/pages.yml）
node_modules/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/

